From cc021c06d29b1492f44ed666d2b688d4cdc17aba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: energie-teilen <noreply@energie-teilen.de>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 20:09:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(engine): metering-concept generator and interval
 allocation engine
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two deterministic engines and the surfaces that use them.

shared/messkonzept.ts derives the metering concept from a constellation:
the variant (Summenzähler / Einzelzähler / Viertelstundenbilanzierung),
the meter inventory with counts and interval-metering flags, the market
roles, an ordered task list with blocking flags, warnings and missing
inputs. Without the grid-connection situation it returns
"not determinable" and names that as the only task, rather than drawing a
concept the inputs do not support. Every result carries the statement
that the network operator's and metering operator's approval is
authoritative.

shared/allocation.ts distributes generation across participants over
fifteen-minute intervals under three keys — static shares, dynamic pro
rata, and static-with-redistribution. Allocation plus feed-in equals
generation in every interval by construction, and no participant is ever
allocated more than they consumed; both invariants are pinned by test,
including across a full year of intervals. compareKeys() runs all three
on one dataset so the difference in self-consumption is computed rather
than asserted. illustrativeDayProfile() and illustrativeShares() produce
a deterministic demonstration profile, labelled as not being measurement.

Surfaces:
- POST /api/v1/messkonzept and POST /api/v1/allocation, listed in
  /api/v1/meta, with the same model stamp and error discipline as the
  existing endpoints; an AllocationError becomes a 400 with its code.
- MesskonzeptPanel with an SVG topology diagram drawn from the same
  result object the inventory table shows.
- AllocationPanel with a day chart and a per-participant coverage
  breakdown, leading with the percentage-point spread between keys.
- The report PDF gains a "Messkonzept und Umsetzungspfad" section with
  the meter inventory, the critical path and the approval statement.

93 new tests; 310 total. Typecheck, tests and build clean.
